### Using the pipe operator

[**Core**]{.core-text}

In your **prac2_exercises.qmd** Quarto document, using the pipe operator, calculate the mean of this vector with `mean()`, find its absolute value with `abs()`, and then round it to the nearest whole number with `round()`. Assign the result to a variable.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
input_vec <- c(5, -10, 4, -3)
```
:::


::: {.callout-answer collapse="true" #ex-pipe_ans}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
input_vec <- c(5, -10, 4, -3)

result <- input_vec |>
  mean() |>
  abs() |>
  round()
```
