For our analysis we will exclude the measurements from the `Spain` site, as this site has no data for the post-Saharan stopover location.

::: {.callout-exercise #ex-filter_breeding .core}

### Filtering a data frame

[**Core**]{.core-text}

In your **worked_example.qmd** Quarto document, filter both the breeding site and the migration site data frames to exclude `Spain` from the `Site` column. Store these in the variables `bird_breeding_exc` and `bird_migration_exc`, respectively.

::: {.callout-answer collapse="true" #ex-filter_breeding_ans}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
bird_breeding_exc <- bird_breeding_selected |>
  filter(Site != "Spain")

bird_migration_exc <- bird_migration_selected |>
  filter(Site != "Spain")

gt(bird_breeding_exc)
```

